      "updated_at": "2026-11-21T20:02:59Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "tACK a02c31c\n\nI first thought `MockableSteadyClock` would be better here, to match #36922 (which uses it for the gbt cache age) and so tests could still control the timeout. But deadline and `now + tick` go into `wait_until`, which waits in real time, so a mocked clock could drift from the actual wait. `steady_clock` is right here, and it matches `WaitTipChanged`.\n\nnit: the rationale from the PR description would be useful in the commit body.\n\nI think this will conflict trivially with my #36940 on the deadline line.",
